# The app asset is a single 3.8 MB HTML file. Two things must not happen to it.
#
# 1. Line-ending translation. Git's autocrlf would rewrite LF to CRLF on a
#    Windows checkout. The file contains base64 data URIs (the résumé, the
#    photo, the icons) and JavaScript string literals; changing bytes inside
#    them corrupts the app. -text turns all translation off.
#
# 2. Diffing. It is one line of 3.1 MB in places. Marking it binary keeps
#    `git diff` and the GitHub web UI from trying to render it, which is what
#    makes a pull request page hang.
*.html -text -diff

# Same reasoning, plus these are genuinely binary.
*.jks binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff2 binary

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they will not run on the CI runner.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.gradle text eol=lf
*.java text eol=lf
*.xml text eol=lf
